<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:29:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Pakistan minister to visit India, but no breakthrough expected</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbad263e975361b7896f254012d1320aaf7ca81c01983c492315e060ecb5ce60</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:29:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717--07503556e8b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Pakistani minister's visit to India for a Shanghai Cooperation Organization forum marks a rare high-level contact between the two archrivals, but analysts say it does not signal a resumption of bilateral engagement.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>APEC summit: Trump, Xi, Putin talks end with 'peace declaration'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2d8be1d331260a319888d8140fd86efaeb04faa6bf30880a945e7ad3e784207</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:29:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/apec-summit-trump-xi-putin-talks-end-with-peace-declaration/live-79964719--35792a5d6dfa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/apec-summit-trump-xi-putin-talks-end-with-peace-declaration/live-79964719?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The three world leaders discussed the Russian invasion of Ukraine as well as nuclear arms controls. Following the trilateral talks, President Trump reportedly headed to the airport. Follow DW live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar committed genocide against Rohingya, top UN court rules</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c50850a557546c6aea5acbc34e5538188ba6891470998439c045f13b1fccb54</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:29:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T11:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-committed-genocide-against-rohingya-top-un-court-rules/a-79987898--1622af9cbda3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-committed-genocide-against-rohingya-top-un-court-rules/a-79987898?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Court of Justice has upheld large parts of a genocide case against Myanmar linked to the 2017 conflict with its Rohingya minority. It called for it to pay reparations and let refugees return safely.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Nearly 50,000 evacuated as Cyclone Akvan nears the coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d6425fbd9b99a19ed5bab79305320c593588b6fcf728693a3585f9205d54583</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:29:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-nearly-50-000-evacuated-as-cyclone-akvan-nears-the-coast/live-79987334--51fef60fd516.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-nearly-50-000-evacuated-as-cyclone-akvan-nears-the-coast/live-79987334?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cyclone Akvan, the third severe storm to hit India's east coast in a month, is expected to make landfall on November 20. Meanwhile, PM Modi led a meeting of his Council of Ministers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea expanded uranium enrichment plant, says IAEA head</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80cbc971956c8e6be2341f8fda7ef16cd405ad3c8cc184bb79d52e8891684486</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-expanded-uranium-enrichment-plant-says-iaea-head/a-79982758--65619f1023d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-expanded-uranium-enrichment-plant-says-iaea-head/a-79982758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">IAEA chief Rafael Grossi has said the ongoing expansion of North Korea's uranium enrichment program remains "a cause for serious concern."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Online censorship grows after 'Cockroach' protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fee952cf6192f11820f1bbeffa69756f06a9d8f4faa75cb255aac4c7d72fa575</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-online-censorship-grows-after-cockroach-protests/a-79976982--a74d2015326f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-online-censorship-grows-after-cockroach-protests/a-79976982?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since anti-government Cockroach protests erupted, journalists and creators say their content is increasingly being restricted on social media in India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>ICJ to rule on Rohingya genocide case against Myanmar: What to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8bd1e8a9175a584648067f58e3ecfadfb19123bda9a5da1b3f9e314aa8519ec</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/icj-to-rule-on-rohingya-genocide-case-against-myanmar-what-to-know/a-79981434--76de3c2375bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/icj-to-rule-on-rohingya-genocide-case-against-myanmar-what-to-know/a-79981434?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ICJ is set to decide whether Myanmar's military operations in Rakhine State a decade ago were carried out with the intent to destroy the country's Rohingya minority, in whole or in part.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Gandhi gives talk in New York, warns of 'looming crisis'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd6956c15786332e16764d2efcd858e187787a9a212f40f9ce3f89c8e1827f47</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T07:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-gandhi-gives-talk-in-new-york-warns-of-looming-crisis/live-79976447--c189b72db73b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-gandhi-gives-talk-in-new-york-warns-of-looming-crisis/live-79976447?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indian opposition leader Rahul Gandhi's US remarks on the economy drew a BJP counterattack. Meanwhile, the Quad leaders pushed back on moves to undermine regional peace,</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's growing exodus of young talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04fc1230a9b4b6eccf5b28998471636109e173b8673d5ef0e25549390734ac5f</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T16:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368--aa300b774c88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflict and uncertainty are driving more and more educated young Iranians to consider leaving the country.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New facilities in Laos and Cambodia: Is China expanding its military presence in Southeast Asia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f23084f70e15045c38c90d9620f3e48e3b151aa8b24fbffc3df3dd43fe5d921</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-facilities-in-laos-and-cambodia-is-china-expanding-its-military-presence-in-southeast-asia/a-79944798--c731be0f2b99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-facilities-in-laos-and-cambodia-is-china-expanding-its-military-presence-in-southeast-asia/a-79944798?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China has been growing its economic relationships in Southeast Asia. Now new military facilities in Laos and Cambodia are causing smaller countries to worry China's military networks are also expanding.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China faces Russia dilemma amid talk of Xi-Trump-Putin summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca2b14490249e0b6885f377f21b3b84b934bb41c3bcf7a4a1c35fe5b5326d5a5</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-faces-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427--86131bd0e961.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-faces-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China is forced to tread carefully as it considers hosting a meeting between Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin, and Donald Trump. While the optics are sure to favor Russia, Beijing is risking its image on the global stage.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's wiretapping scandal opens political fault line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5bed9d39a641447d13bd6b033b870dbee08c7a480dd54ce67069e74d3496d00</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-political-fault-line/a-79939753--1c825a485886.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-political-fault-line/a-79939753?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senior police officers are accused of illegally monitoring President Prabowo Subianto, exposing rival networks within Indonesia's security establishment and renewing concerns about political misuse of surveillance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
